{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a stitch task (#5333) from the cobbler-scaffold pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd035-rmdir requirements R4.1, R4.2, and R4.3, which are the \"Differential testing\" requirements for the `cmd/rmdir` utility. Specifically:\n   - R4.1: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and grmdir via pkg/testutils\n   - R4.2: Tests must cover: single empty directory removal, multiple directories, -p with nested empty directories, non-empty directory error, non-existent directory error, --ignore-fail-on-non-empty suppression, and -v verbose output\n   - R4.3: Tests must verify that -p stops ascending correctly when a parent is not empty, matching grmdir behavior\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/rmdir/main.go` and `cmd/rmdir/rmdir_test.go`. The task requires verifying against acceptance criteria AC1-AC5 (compilation and test passing).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (grmdir from Homebrew coreutils)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests and DiffTest struct for test infrastructure\n   - testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") for building the Go binary under test\n   - exec.LookPath(\"grmdir\") with t.Skip for graceful skip when reference binary missing\n   - sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main\n   - syscall.Rmdir for directory removal, syscall.ENOTEMPTY for non-empty detection\n   - Binary name normalization in tests via regexp to compare output regardless of binary path\n   - Custom runBin/compareResults helpers alongside RunDiffTests for tests that need filesystem setup in separate directories\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd035-rmdir.yaml`\n     - The SRD specification defining all requirements R1-R4 and acceptance criteria AC1-AC6\n     - R4 (Differential testing) has three sub-items: R4.1 (compare stdout/stderr/exit), R4.2 (test coverage list), R4.3 (-p stop ascending verification)\n     - Non-goals: no non-empty removal, no file arguments, no stdin input\n\n   - `cmd/rmdir/main.go` (186 lines)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R3.4 completely\n     - Has options struct (parents, verbose, ignoreFailOnNonEmpty), parseArgs with short/long flag support\n     - run() function processes directories, handles -p parent removal, --ignore-fail-on-non-empty, -v verbose\n     - isNonEmptyError checks syscall.ENOTEMPTY\n     - sysErrMsg translates errno to human-readable strings\n     - Full existing implementation:\n     ```go\n     func run(opts options, dirs []string) int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, dir := range dirs {\n             if err := syscall.Rmdir(dir); err != nil {\n                 if opts.ignoreFailOnNonEmpty && isNonEmptyError(err) {\n                     if opts.verbose {\n                         fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"rmdir: removing directory, '%s'\\n\", dir)\n                     }\n                     continue\n                 }\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rmdir: failed to remove '%s': %s\\n\", dir, sysErrMsg(err))\n                 exitCode = 1\n                 continue\n             }\n             if opts.verbose {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"rmdir: removing directory, '%s'\\n\", dir)\n             }\n             if opts.parents {\n                 for parent := filepath.Dir(filepath.Clean(dir)); parent != \".\" && parent != \"/\"; parent = filepath.Dir(parent) {\n                     if err := syscall.Rmdir(parent); err != nil {\n                         if opts.ignoreFailOnNonEmpty && isNonEmptyError(err) { break }\n                         fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rmdir: failed to remove directory '%s': %s\\n\", parent, sysErrMsg(err))\n                         exitCode = 1\n                         break\n                     }\n                     if opts.verbose {\n                         fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"rmdir: removing directory, '%s'\\n\", parent)\n                     }\n                 }\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/rmdir/rmdir_test.go` (333 lines)\n     - Already has extensive test infrastructure: runRemovalTest, binResult, runBin, compareResults helpers\n     - Uses context.WithTimeout for 10s timeout on binary execution\n     - normalizeBinaryName regex replaces binary paths with \"rmdir\"\n     - Already covers many R4.2 scenarios: no_args, nonexistent, not_a_directory, nonempty, single_empty, multiple_empty, partial_failure, multiple_nonexistent, parents_nested_empty, parents_stop_at_nonempty, parents_multiple_args, parents_single_dir, parents_nonexistent, ignore_nonempty, ignore_nonexistent, ignore_with_parents_nonempty_ancestor, verbose_single, verbose_multiple, verbose_parents, verbose_with_ignore\n     - Key helper:\n     ```go\n     func runBin(t *testing.T, binary string, args []string, workDir string) binResult {\n         t.Helper()\n         ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second)\n         defer cancel()\n         cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, binary, args...)\n         cmd.Dir = workDir\n         cmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), \"LC_ALL=C\")\n         // ... captures stdout, stderr, exit code\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was still in the reading/planning phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The task requires implementing R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 which are test requirements. The existing test file already has significant coverage. The work needed is to:\n     1. Verify all R4.2 coverage items are present and add any missing test cases\n     2. Ensure R4.3 is properly test